lls back to `npm install` and surfaces a warning. Once the offending package republishes a clean version you can switch back with `pnpm install`.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01M2gq4ULyVBpxdfwxwJ5Nks","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
