{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019rfnEPYSqKN4vGBeDgzZw1","type":"tool_result","content":"prisma db init → Bootstrap a database to match the current contract and sign it\n\n│  Usage\n│    $ prisma db init [options]\n│\n│  Creates everything the emitted contract declares and the database does not\n│  have yet, using additive operations only. Structures already in place and\n│  compatible are left alone, a conflict that would need a destructive change\n│  stops the run, and the database is signed with the contract it now matches.\n│  Use --dry-run to see the operations without applying them.\n│\n│  Options\n│      --db <url>            Database connection string\n│      --dry-run             Preview the planned operations without applying them\n│      --advance-ref <name>  Advance the named ref to the post-command contract hash\n│\n│  Global options also apply: --format, --json, --log-level, --verbose,\n│  --quiet, --yes, --confirm, --interactive, --color, --config. Run 'prisma\n│  --help' for details.\n│\n│  Examples\n│    $ prisma db init\n│    $ prisma db init --db $DATABASE_URL\n│    $ prisma db init --dry-run\n│    $ prisma db init --advance-ref production\n│\n│  Docs  https://docs.prisma.io/docs/orm/v8/reference/error-reference/\n\nPrisma agent skills are out of date (installed @prisma/orm-postgres 8.0.0-rc.23, synced none). Run: prisma skills sync","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"700e731c-4d50-4e33-b204-47a51f78e9ad","uuid":"7a9c91ac-d090-4eee-8a73-2c2d372a84f9","timestamp":"2026-11-10T03:05:58.084Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"prisma db init → Bootstrap a database to match the current contract and sign it\n\n│  Usage\n│    $ prisma db init [options]\n│\n│  Creates everything the emitted contract declares and the database does not\n│  have yet, using additive operations only. Structures already in place and\n│  compatible are left alone, a conflict that would need a destructive change\n│  sto